          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tóuyūn is built from 头 'head' and yūn, both inherited from Middle Chinese, duw and hjunH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second as a halo round the sun or moon. The level tone of yūn is irregular, and the sense 'dizzy' is not given there."
            }
          ]
